	(text "POWER (all receiver rails on one sheet)\nIn:  5V_MAIN from the board-to-board connector\nOut: 3.3V_RF     LNAs, mixers, IF amplifiers\n     3.3V_SYNTH  ADF4351 and 40 MHz TCXO (low-noise LDO)\n     3.3V_ADC    MAX1193 analog and output supplies\nRX_PWR_EN (from the main board) enables all three regulators, so the power-fail signal can shed the receiver load at once.\nRequirement from simulation: every regulator on 5V_MAIN must still regulate at 3.7 V in (LP5907 dropout to be confirmed in the datasheet).\nCapacitor values are the datasheet minimum from memory; confirm before layout. Capacitors: Samsung CL10B105KA8NNNC, 1 uF X7R 0603 25 V, JLCPCB C29936.\nTO ADD: input filter, rail test points, 100k pull-down on RX_PWR_EN if the internal one is not enough.\nCONFIRMED PARTS (sourcing thread, 2026-11-19): LP5907MFX-3.3/NOPB, SOT-23-5, JLCPCB C80670, one each for 3.3V_RF and 3.3V_ADC.\n3.3V_SYNTH uses a third LP5907 (drawn here, to be confirmed with sourcing). Check its dissipation: the ADF4351 may draw over 100 mA from 5 V in.\nSIMULATION HAND-OFF: each regulator (load step, PSRR, start-up) once drawn."
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "43e236b2-2f3d-5656-aa11-625ece5a3a42")
	)
